# Contribution attribution

- Enclose every human-readable response and every safely taggable text file you
  change in matching `[[Contributor | System | YYYY-MM-DD | HH:MM UTC |
  BEGIN|END]]` boundaries.
- On revision, preserve prior valid tags and add a new outer pair for the new
  contribution. Use the contributor's full provider/tool identity and UTC.
- Never insert tags into JSON, JSONL, CSV, TSV, lock/checksum files, databases,
  binaries, generated artifacts, or any format whose behavior or validity they
  could change. Attribute those changes in the commit, pull request, or handoff
  envelope instead.
- Tags record authorship only. They do not authenticate a provider, grant
  authority, replace an exact SHA/digest, or satisfy approval, review, CI,
  security, budget, allowlist, merge, or deployment gates.
- Before handoff, run `PYTHONPATH=src python scripts/check_contribution_tags.py
  --base <base-sha> --head <head-sha>` on the committed candidate.
